        },
        {
          "afterOffset": 14139,
          "afterBytes": 83,
          "beforeText": "\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<option id=\"scspCustomFmOption\" value=\"custom\" disabled>Custom · 2OP</option>\n"
        },
        {
          "afterOffset": 16030,
          "afterBytes": 275,
          "beforeText": "\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<label>Modulation from\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<select id=\"scspCustomFmInput\"><option value=\"\">None</option><option value=\"0\">A</option><option value=\"1\">B</option></select>\n"
        },
        {
          "afterOffset": 16324,
          "afterBytes": 336,
          "beforeText": ""
        },
        {
          "afterOffset": 16824,
          "afterBytes": 900,
          "beforeText": "\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<summary aria-label=\"About custom two-operator connections\">?</summary>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>Choose A or B above, then its modulation source and direct output. An operator can both modulate another and produce sound. Clear the existing input before reversing a connection.</p>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>This graph editor and its voice allocation are Synth software over SCSP slot modulation. The initial Custom editor accepts acyclic 2OP connections. Self modulation, loops and Custom 4/6OP are follow-up work; raw physical CH controls keep their existing behavior.</p>\n"
        },
        {
          "afterOffset": 41575,
          "afterBytes": 189,
          "beforeText": "\t\t\t\t\t\tPairs / Branch support 2 / 4 / 6 operators; Custom starts with acyclic 2OP.\n\t\t\t\t\t\tCustom 4/6OP and FM feedback are future work. The editor core uses zero slot-write delay. SSF\n"
        },
        {
          "afterOffset": 42137,
          "afterBytes": 67,
          "beforeText": "\t\t<script type=\"module\" src=\"synth.js?v=scsp-fm-custom2-1\"></script>\n"
        }
